# Facts of the N0a playtest-scenario-trust ladder in middleware_pipeline.py's _reset_write_caches.
# scenarioUncertainNext answers what Middleware._scenario_uncertain becomes after this response.
# sceneInvalidateGate answers whether invalidate_scene_caches() must run. Deliberately two decisions,
# not one: N0a-3's give-up path (forceInvalidateFlag) must invalidate caches WITHOUT clearing the
# uncertain guard (Unity's actual stop is unproven), which falls out for free when the two concerns
# are kept separate instead of forced into one combined ladder.
#
# Out of scope (assessed, not forced into this DECISION): the belt-and-suspenders duplicate at the
# top of wrapped() (a single boolean, not a ladder), the except-clause invalidate on a wire exception
# during a PLAYTEST_SCENARIO_CMDS command (control-flow coupled, no result to build facts from), and
# track_editor_state's edit-mode-off clear in middleware_reads.py (a different concern -- play-state
# tracking, not playtest-ack/terminal tracking -- that happens to touch the same field).
CONTRACT unitymcp.scenarionext
COVERAGE declared-scope
MODULE scenarionext_facts
FACT scn.cmdIsStartPlaytest bool
FACT scn.resultIsRunIdAck bool
FACT scn.resultIsTerminal bool
FACT scn.forceInvalidateFlag bool
INPUT scenarioUncertainNext scn.cmdIsStartPlaytest scn.resultIsRunIdAck scn.resultIsTerminal
INPUT sceneInvalidateGate scn.resultIsTerminal scn.forceInvalidateFlag
